WEBVTT

00:00.280 --> 00:00.950
Well done.

00:00.950 --> 00:05.120
You've made it to Chapter 4, which means you're halfway through the course.

00:05.120 --> 00:06.570
You can read a graph,

00:06.570 --> 00:09.900
describe trends and use the grammar accurately.

00:09.900 --> 00:12.240
There are three chapters left:

00:12.240 --> 00:13.730
comparisons,

00:13.730 --> 00:15.520
putting your answer together,

00:15.520 --> 00:17.630
and then your timed practice.

00:17.630 --> 00:20.870
Look at what the task actually asks you to do:

00:20.870 --> 00:26.040
summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features,

00:26.040 --> 00:29.180
and make comparisons where relevant.

00:29.180 --> 00:31.970
So that's three jobs: select,

00:31.970 --> 00:32.910
describe

00:32.910 --> 00:33.730
and compare.

00:34.140 --> 00:35.710
As a former IELTS examiner,

00:35.710 --> 00:38.730
I'd look for all three under Task Achievement.

00:38.730 --> 00:40.320
A very common mistake is

00:40.320 --> 00:42.470
listing the numbers for each line,

00:42.470 --> 00:45.300
one after another, with no comparison.

00:45.300 --> 00:46.810
Every figure can be right,

00:46.810 --> 00:49.390
and the answer still misses part of the task.

00:50.060 --> 00:52.020
So let's start comparing,

00:52.020 --> 00:55.930
and the first rule is simple: compare like with like.

00:55.930 --> 00:59.030
This graph shows how much water one person

00:59.030 --> 01:02.450
used each day in three towns.

01:02.450 --> 01:04.650
Here's a sentence that sounds fine at first:

01:05.170 --> 01:08.190
"Northport was higher than Easton's water use."

01:08.190 --> 01:09.770
Read both sides of "than".

01:09.770 --> 01:12.230
On the left, Northport. That's a town.

01:12.230 --> 01:15.700
On the right, Easton's water use. That's a figure.

01:15.700 --> 01:17.600
So we're comparing a town with a number,

01:17.600 --> 01:20.350
and that doesn't work.

01:20.350 --> 01:22.510
There are three easy fixes.

01:22.510 --> 01:26.880
Water use in Northport was higher than in Easton.

01:26.880 --> 01:29.880
Northport's water use was higher than Easton's.

01:29.880 --> 01:31.400
Or, more formally:

01:31.400 --> 01:35.910
the figure for Northport was higher than that for Easton.

01:35.910 --> 01:38.060
"That for" means "the figure for".

01:38.060 --> 01:40.000
Now it's a figure against a figure:

01:40.000 --> 01:44.100
in 2004, 150 litres against 90.

01:44.100 --> 01:45.410
So when you compare,

01:45.410 --> 01:48.520
read both sides of "than" or "compared with".

01:48.520 --> 01:49.970
Same kind of thing?

01:49.970 --> 01:50.870
Great.

01:50.870 --> 01:53.250
A place on one side and a number on the other?

01:53.250 --> 01:54.520
Rewrite it.

01:54.520 --> 01:57.100
Now try the questions on the next page.

